[0.5397, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[1;1H\u001b[0m  ├────────────────┼────────────────────────┤\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[2;1H\u001b[0m  │ Standard       │ Yes (S), active        │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[3;1H\u001b[0m  └────────────────┴────────────────────────┘\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[4;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[5;1H\u001b[0m  \"Heart attack\" is a recorded synonym of this concept, so it came back as an exact match.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[6;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[7;1H\u001b[0m  The lookup also returned \u001b[0;1m4134723, Coronary artery thrombosis\u001b[0m. It only matched because a broader non-standard concept,\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[8;1H\u001b[0m  \"Myocardial infarction (& [acute]) or coronary thrombosis\" (40345176), maps to it. That makes it a weaker match, so\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[9;1H\u001b[0m  4329847 is the one to use.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[10;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[11;1H\u001b[0m  If you're building a cohort, use 4329847 with its descendants so that more specific types, such as acute MI, are\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[12;1H\u001b[0m  included.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[13;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[14;1H\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[0m \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mBaked for 17s · done 6:57 pm\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[15;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[16;1H\u001b[0;38;2;122;162;247;48;2;28;46;82m❯ \u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255;48;2;28;46;82mWhich drugs make up the FOLFOX regimen, as OMOP standard RxNorm ingredients?\u001b[0;48;2;28;46;82m                                          \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[17;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[18;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mCalled groundworkers \u001b[0;1;38;2;153;153;153m2\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m times \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[19;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[20;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m FOLFOX is made up of three drugs, each a standard RxNorm ingredient:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[21;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[22;1H\u001b[0m  ┌──────────────┬────────────┬────────────────────┬──────────┐\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[23;1H\u001b[0m  │     Drug     │ concept_id │ Vocabulary / class │ Standard │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[24;1H\u001b[0m  ├──────────────┼────────────┼────────────────────┼──────────┤\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[25;1H\u001b[0m  │ fluorouracil │ \u001b[0;1m955632\u001b[0m     │ RxNorm Ingredient  │ S        │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[26;1H\u001b[0m  ├──────────────┼────────────┼────────────────────┼──────────┤\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[0m  │ leucovorin   │ \u001b[0;1m1388796\u001b[0m    │ RxNorm Ingredient  │ S        │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[28;1H\u001b[0m  ├──────────────┼────────────┼────────────────────┼──────────┤\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[29;1H\u001b[0m  │ oxaliplatin  │ \u001b[0;1m1318011\u001b[0m    │ RxNorm Ingredient  │ S        │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[0m  └──────────────┴────────────┴────────────────────┴──────────┘\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[31;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[32;1H\u001b[0m  These come from the HemOnc regimen concept \u001b[0;1mFOLFOX (35806596)\u001b[0m, through its \"Has cytotox chemo Rx\" relationships. The\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[33;1H\u001b[0m  regimen also links to HemOnc component concepts (35803077, 35803081, 35803227). Those are non-standard, so don't use\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[34;1H\u001b[0m  them for drug exposure queries.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[35;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[36;1H\u001b[0m  - \u001b[0;1mBuilding a cohort:\u001b[0m include the descendants of each ingredient so that clinical and branded drug records are\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[37;1H\u001b[0m    captured.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[38;1H\u001b[0m  - \u001b[0;1mLeucovorin variants:\u001b[0m if your data records levoleucovorin as a substitute, it is a separate ingredient and isn't one\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[39;1H\u001b[0m    of the three above.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[0m  - \u001b[0;1mFOLFOX chronotherapy:\u001b[0m this is a separate regimen concept (35804808). I didn't check its components.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[41;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[42;1H\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153