[0.5997, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[1;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m FOLFOX is made up of three drugs, each a standard RxNorm ingredient:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[2;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[3;1H\u001b[0m  ┌──────────────┬────────────┬────────────────────┬──────────┐\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[4;1H\u001b[0m  │     Drug     │ concept_id │ Vocabulary / class │ Standard │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[5;1H\u001b[0m  ├──────────────┼────────────┼────────────────────┼──────────┤\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[6;1H\u001b[0m  │ fluorouracil │ \u001b[0;1m955632\u001b[0m     │ RxNorm Ingredient  │ S        │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[7;1H\u001b[0m  ├──────────────┼────────────┼────────────────────┼──────────┤\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[8;1H\u001b[0m  │ leucovorin   │ \u001b[0;1m1388796\u001b[0m    │ RxNorm Ingredient  │ S        │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[9;1H\u001b[0m  ├──────────────┼────────────┼────────────────────┼──────────┤\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[10;1H\u001b[0m  │ oxaliplatin  │ \u001b[0;1m1318011\u001b[0m    │ RxNorm Ingredient  │ S        │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[11;1H\u001b[0m  └──────────────┴────────────┴────────────────────┴──────────┘\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[12;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[13;1H\u001b[0m  These come from the HemOnc regimen concept \u001b[0;1mFOLFOX (35806596)\u001b[0m, through its \"Has cytotox chemo Rx\" relationships. The\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[14;1H\u001b[0m  regimen also links to HemOnc component concepts (35803077, 35803081, 35803227). Those are non-standard, so don't use\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[15;1H\u001b[0m  them for drug exposure queries.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[16;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[17;1H\u001b[0m  - \u001b[0;1mBuilding a cohort:\u001b[0m include the descendants of each ingredient so that clinical and branded drug records are\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[18;1H\u001b[0m    captured.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[19;1H\u001b[0m  - \u001b[0;1mLeucovorin variants:\u001b[0m if your data records levoleucovorin as a substitute, it is a separate ingredient and isn't one\u001b[0m