[0.1919, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[1;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[2;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mRan \u001b[0;1;38;2;153;153;153m3\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m shell commands \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[3;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[4;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m I've built the colorectal cancer concept set: \u001b[0;1m1,455 standard concepts\u001b[0m in six anatomical groups, plus an optional\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[5;1H\u001b[0m  appendix group of 118. It is an explicit list of concepts, so in ATLAS or Capr import it as-is with \"include\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[6;1H\u001b[0m  descendants\" turned off. Turning descendants on for broad parents like 443396 would bring the excluded lymphomas and\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[7;1H\u001b[0m  in situ codes back in.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[8;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[9;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mFiles:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[10;1H\u001b[0m  - Included concepts: /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-XXXXXXXX-Documents-CODE-agent-stack/a15ebb57-383e-474c-8d15-90a2e6\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[11;1H\u001b[0m    60d5c7/scratchpad/crc/crc_concept_set_included.csv\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[12;1H\u001b[0m  - Excluded concepts, each with a reason: /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-XXXXXXXX-Documents-CODE-agent-stack/a15ebb57-3\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[13;1H\u001b[0m    83e-474c-8d15-90a2e660d5c7/scratchpad/crc/crc_concept_set_excluded.csv\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[14;1H\u001b[0m  - Script that rebuilds both: /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-XXXXXXXX-Documents-CODE-agent-stack/a15ebb57-383e-474c-8d1\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[15;1H\u001b[0m    5-90a2e660d5c7/scratchpad/crc/build.py\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[17;1H\u001b[0m  Each row has a \u001b[0;38;2;177;185;249mregion\u001b[0m and a finer \u001b[0;38;2;177;185;249msegment\u001b[0m column, so you can regroup it, for example by individual colon segment.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[18;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[19;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mHow it was built:\u001b[0m I took all standard descendants of \u001b[0;1mMalignant tumor of large intestine (443396, SNOMED)\u001b[0m, 2,329\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[20;1H\u001b[0m  concepts at full depth, and sorted each one into a region. The ICD-O-3 site codes (C18.x, C19.9, C20.9) gave the\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[21;1H\u001b[0m  region for ICD-O-3 concepts; the site named in the concept name gave it for SNOMED ones.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[23;1H\u001b[0m  ┌────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┬─────┐\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[24;1H\u001b[0m  │         Group          │                 Includes                 │          Key parent concepts          │  n  │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[25;1H\u001b[0m  ├────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────┤\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[26;1H\u001b[0m  │ 1. Right (proximal)    │ Cecum (and ileocecal valve), ascending   │ 443391 cecum, 435754 ascending,       │     │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[0m  │ colon                  │ colon, hepatic flexure, transverse colon │ 4180791 hepatic flexure, 443384       │ 464 │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[28;1H\u001b[0m  │                        │                                          │ transverse                            │     │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[29;1H\u001b[0m  ├────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────┤\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[0m  │ 2. Left (distal) colon │ Splenic flexure, descending colon,       │ 4181344 splenic flexure, 443382       │ 353 │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[31;1H\u001b[0m  │                        │ sigmoid colon                            │ descending, 443381 sigmoid            │     │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[32;1H\u001b[0m  ├────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────┤\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[33;1H\u001b[0m  │ 3. Colon, overlapping  │ Colon NOS, overlapping lesions of colon  │ 4180790 