 │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[14;1H\u001b[0m  └───────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────┴─────┘\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[15;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[16;1H\u001b[0m  I put the transverse colon in the right colon, following the usual split at the splenic flexure. Moving it is a\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[17;1H\u001b[0m  one-line change in the script.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[18;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[19;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mExcluded (842 concepts):\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[20;1H\u001b[0m  - \u001b[0;1mNon-solid tumours (782):\u001b[0m every ICD-O-3 haematolymphoid code (histology 9590–9999), plus Lymphoma of colon\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[21;1H\u001b[0m    (37018876), of sigmoid colon (40486168) and of appendix (603015).\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[22;1H\u001b[0m  - \u001b[0;1mNon-malignant (29):\u001b[0m in situ codes (ICD-O-3 behaviour /2). Benign and uncertain-behaviour concepts aren't under the\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[23;1H\u001b[0m    malignant parent, so they were never pulled in.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[24;1H\u001b[0m  - \u001b[0;1mAnal (25):\u001b[0m 23 ICD-O-3 cloacogenic-zone (C21.2) codes that the hierarchy files under rectum, plus 4095430 and 438090,\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[25;1H\u001b[0m    which combine rectum with anus.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[26;1H\u001b[0m  - \u001b[0;1mSecondary involvement (7):\u001b[0m \"Malignant tumor involving rectum by direct extension from…\" ovary, prostate, cervix and\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[0m    so on. These are other cancers spreading into the rectum.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[28;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[29;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mChoices you may want to revisit:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[0m  1. \u001b[0;1mAppendix:\u001b[0m ICD-10 puts it inside C18, but most colorectal cancer definitions leave it out. Drop or keep that group\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[31;1H\u001b[0m     as you need.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[32;1H\u001b[0m  2. \u001b[0;1mSolid tumours other than 