ndix (603015).\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[17;1H\u001b[0m  - \u001b[0;1mNon-malignant (29):\u001b[0m in situ codes (ICD-O-3 behaviour /2). Benign and uncertain-behaviour concepts aren't under the\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[18;1H\u001b[0m    malignant parent, so they were never pulled in.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[19;1H\u001b[0m  - \u001b[0;1mAnal (25):\u001b[0m 23 ICD-O-3 cloacogenic-zone (C21.2) codes that the hierarchy files under rectum, plus 4095430 and 438090,\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[20;1H\u001b[0m    which combine rectum with anus.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[21;1H\u001b[0m  - \u001b[0;1mSecondary involvement (7):\u001b[0m \"Malignant tumor involving rectum by direct extension from…\" ovary, prostate, cervix and\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[22;1H\u001b[0m    so on. These are other cancers spreading into the rectum.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[23;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[24;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mChoices you may want to revisit:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[25;1H\u001b[0m  1. \u001b[0;1mAppendix:\u001b[0m ICD-10 puts it inside C18, but most colorectal cancer definitions leave it out. Drop or keep that group\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[26;1H\u001b[0m     as you need.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[0m  2. \u001b[0;1mSolid tumours other than carcinoma are kept:\u001b[0m neuroendocrine tumours, GIST, sarcomas, Kaposi sarcoma (608057) and\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[28;1H\u001b[0m     melanoma of rectum (4171274). If you want carcinoma or adenocarcinoma only, I can filter by ICD-O-3 histology and\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[29;1H\u001b[0m     SNOMED name.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[0m  3. \u001b[0;1mNot included:\u001b[0m MedDRA \"colorectal cancer\" terms, because they're non-standard, and secondary (metastatic) neoplasms\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[31;1H\u001b[0m     of the colon or rectum.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[32;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[33;1H\u001b[0m  I can also turn this into an ATLAS concept-set JSON per group, or check it against the CQI library with\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[34;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b