[K\u001b[38;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[39;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mCalled groundworkers \u001b[0;1;38;2;153;153;153m9\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m times \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[41;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m I found a real gap: 44502762 (large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma of ascending colon) is a standard concept but isn't\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[42;1H\u001b[0m  a descendant of 443396, since not all ICD-O-3 concepts attach to the SNOMED hierarchy. I'll instead sweep all ICD-O-3\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[43;1H\u001b[0m  concepts for the ascending colon by name rather than relying on hierarchy.\u001b[0m\u001b[K"]
