eady included.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[20;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[21;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mCalled groundworkers \u001b[0;1;38;2;153;153;153m9\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m times \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[22;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[23;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m I found a real gap: 44502762 (large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma of ascending colon) is a standard concept but isn't\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[24;1H\u001b[0m  a descendant of 443396, since not all ICD-O-3 concepts attach to the SNOMED hierarchy. I'll instead sweep all ICD-O-3\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[25;1H\u001b[0m  concepts for the ascending colon by name rather than relying on hierarchy.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[26;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mCalled groundworkers \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[28;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[29;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m Since full-text search caps out around 50 results, I'll cross-check the returned results against the set and then look\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[0m  up each of the 41 histologies found at other colorectal sites but missing at C18.2 individually.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[31;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[32;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mRan \u001b[0;1;38;2;153;153;153m1\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m shell command \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[33;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[34;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m Those 7 entries are correctly excluded, covering benign, uncertain-behaviour, in situ, inactive, and metastatic cases.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[35;1H\u001b[0m  Moving on to the remaining histology lookups.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[36;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[37;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mCalled groundworkers \u001b[0;1;38;2;153;153;153m33\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m times \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[38;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[39;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m I found one real gap among the 41 histology codes — 8013/3, 44502762 — while three others map to SNOMED concepts\u001b[