[0.0352, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[1;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[3;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mCalled groundworkers \u001b[0;1;38;2;153;153;153m4\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m times \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[4;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[5;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m Those weren't true gaps — 8140/3, 8000/3, and 8010/3 at C18.2 exist but are non-standard, mapped to a standard concept\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[6;1H\u001b[0m  via \"Maps to.\" Now checking where all 41 missing histology codes map and whether those targets are already included.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[7;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[8;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mCalled groundworkers \u001b[0;1;38;2;153;153;153m9\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m times \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[9;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[10;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m I found a real gap: 44502762 (large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma of ascending colon) is a standard concept but isn't\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[11;1H\u001b[0m  a descendant of 443396, since not all ICD-O-3 concepts attach to the SNOMED hierarchy. I'll instead sweep all ICD-O-3\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[12;1H\u001b[0m  concepts for the ascending colon by name rather than relying on hierarchy.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[13;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[14;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mCalled groundworkers \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[15;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[16;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m Since full-text search caps out around 50 results, I'll cross-check the returned results against the set and then look\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[17;1H\u001b[0m  up each of the 41 histologies found at other colorectal sites but missing at C18.2 individually.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[18;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[19;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mRan \u001b[0;1;38;2;153;153;153m1\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m shell command \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[20;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[21;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m Those 7 entries are correctly excluded, covering benign, uncertain-behaviour, in situ, inactive, and metastatic cases.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[22;1H\u001b[0m  Moving on to the remaining histology lookups.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[23;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[24;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mCalled groundworkers \u001b[0;1;38;2;153;153;153m33\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m times \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[25;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[26;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m I found one real gap among the 41 histology codes — 8013/3, 44502762 — while three others map to SNOMED concepts\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[0m  already included and 36 combinations don't exist at C18.2. Next I'll investigate why 44502762 is disconnected from the\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[28;1H\u001b[0m  hierarchy and check the SNOMED side.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[29;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mCalled groundworkers \u001b[0;1;38;2;153;153;153m3\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m times \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[31;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[32;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m Found that codes 761001 and 760999 sit under Neoplasm of ascending colon but not under Malignant tumor of large\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[33;1H\u001b[0m  intestine, so they're missing from the set — I'll verify thoroughly by diffing everything under Neoplasm of ascending\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[34;1H\u001b[0m  colon (4130997) against the set.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[35;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[36;1H\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m⏺\u001b[0m Calling groundworkers, running \u001b[0;1m1\u001b[0m shell command…\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[37;1H\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  $ SP=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-XXXXXXXX-Documents-CODE-agent-stack/a15ebb57-383e-474c-8d15-90a2e660d5c7/scratc\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[38;1H\u001b[0m     \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mhpad/crc\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[39;1H\u001b[0m     \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mpython3 -I - $SP /Users/XXXXXXXX/.claude/projects/-Users-XXXXXXXX-Documents-CODE-agent-stack/a15ebb57-383e-474c-8d1\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[0m     \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m5-90a2e660d5c7/tool-results/mcp-groundworkers-concept_descen…\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[41;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[42;1H\u001b[0;38;2;215;119;87m✽\u001b[0m \u001b[0;38;2;215;119;87mDilly\u001b[0;38;2;235;159;127m-da\u001b[0;38;2;215;119;87mllying… \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m(1m 44s · ↓\u001b[0m \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m11.2k tokens)\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[43;1H\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Tip: Use /btw to ask a quick side question without interrupting Claude's current work\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[44;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K"]
[0.096, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[36;1H\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m⏺\u001b[0m Confirming every included ascending concept sits under the ascending colon neoplasm hierarchy\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[42;1H\u001b[0;38;2;215;119;87m✽\u001b[0m \u001b[0;38;2;215;119;87mDilly-dallying… \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m(2m 2s · ↓\u001b[0m \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m12.3k tokens · thought for 8s)\u001b[0m\u001b[K"]
[0.1314, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[3;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m Found that codes 761001 and 760999 sit under Neoplasm of ascending colon but not under Malignant tumor of large\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[4;1H\u001b[0m  intestine, so they're missing from the set — I'll verify thoroughly by diffing everything under Neoplasm of ascending\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[5;1H\u001b[0m  colon (4130997) against the set.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[6;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[7;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mCalled groundworkers, ran \u001b[0;1;38;2;153;153;153m2\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m shell commands \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[8;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[9;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m The ascending colon group is missing \u001b[0;1m2 malignant concepts\u001b[0m; everything else checks out. Both gaps come from a break in\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[10;1H\u001b[0m  the vocabulary hierarchy, not from the exclusion rules.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[11;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[12;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mMissing; should be added:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[14;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mconcept_id:\u001b[0m \u001b[0;1m761001\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[15;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mName:\u001b[0m Primary malignant neuroendocrine neoplasm of ascending colon\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[16;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mVocab / code:\u001b[0m SNOMED 130381000119103\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[17;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mWhy it was missed:\u001b[0m Its parent, \u001b[0;1m760999\u001b[0m \"Primary malignant neuroendocrine neoplasm of large intestine\", sits under\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[18;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;3mNeoplasm of large intestine\u001b[0m but not under \u001b[0;3mMalignant tumor of large intestine\u001b[0m (443396), which is where I built the set\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[19;1H\u001b[0m   from\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[20;1H\u001b[0m  ────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[21;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mconcept_id:\u001b[0m \u001b[0;1m44502762\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[22;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mName:\u001b[0m Large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma of ascending colon\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[23;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mVocab / code:\u001b[0m ICD-O-3 8013/3-C18.2\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[24;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mWhy it was missed:\u001b[0m It is a child of 761001, so it is missing for the same reason\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[26;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mHow I checked:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[28;1H\u001b[0m  1. \u001b[0;1mFull sweep of the anatomy hierarchy:\u001b[0m I took all 420 standard descendants of \u001b[0;1mNeoplasm of ascending colon (4130997)\u001b[0m,\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[29;1H\u001b[0m     which covers every behaviour (benign, in situ, uncertain, malignant), and diffed them against the set. 54 were not\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[0m     in either the included or excluded file. 52 of those are correctly left out:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[31;1H\u001b[0m     - 24 benign: 22 ICD-O-3 /0 codes, plus Benign neoplasm (442111) and Adenoma (46273188)\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[32;1H\u001b[0m     - 19 in situ: 18 ICD-O-3 /2 codes, plus Carcinoma in situ (4243742)\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[33;1H\u001b[0m     - 5 uncertain behaviour: 4 ICD-O-3 /1 codes, plus 4313363\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[34;1H\u001b[0m     - 4 hepatic flexure concepts that are benign, in situ, uncertain or unspecified neoplasm (4129878, 4241044,\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[35;1H\u001b[0m       4243126, 4315411)\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[36;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[37;1H\u001b[0m     The other two are the gaps in the table.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[38;1H\u001b[0m  2. \u001b[0;1mThe other direction:\u001b[0m all 117 included ascending concepts sit under 4130997, so none is misassigned to this segment.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[39;1H\u001b[0m  3. \u001b[0;1mHistology coverage:\u001b[0m 41 ICD-O-3 histologies exist at other colorectal sites but not at C18.2. I looked each one up\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[0m     by code:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[41;1H\u001b[0m     - \u001b[0;1m1 is a real gap\u001b[0m: 8013/3, already in the table above.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[42;1H\u001b[0m     - \u001b[0;1m4 are non-standard\u001b[0m: 8000/3, 8010/3, 8140/3 and 8241/3. Each maps to a standard concept already in the set\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[43;1H\u001b[0m       (4247719, 4207182, 36713361 and 760958). One of them, \u001b[0;1m8140/3 Adenocarcinoma NOS\u001b[0m, is the most common colorectal\u001b[0m\u001b[K"]
