[0.0188, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[1;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m The ascending colon group is missing \u001b[0;1m2 malignant concepts\u001b[0m; everything else checks out. Both gaps come from a break in\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[2;1H\u001b[0m  the vocabulary hierarchy, not from the exclusion rules.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[3;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[4;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mMissing; should be added:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[5;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[6;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mconcept_id:\u001b[0m \u001b[0;1m761001\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[7;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mName:\u001b[0m Primary malignant neuroendocrine neoplasm of ascending colon\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[8;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mVocab / code:\u001b[0m SNOMED 130381000119103\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[9;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mWhy it was missed:\u001b[0m Its parent, \u001b[0;1m760999\u001b[0m \"Primary malignant neuroendocrine neoplasm of large intestine\", sits under\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[10;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;3mNeoplasm of large intestine\u001b[0m but not under \u001b[0;3mMalignant tumor of large intestine\u001b[0m (443396), which is where I built the set\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[11;1H\u001b[0m   from\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[12;1H\u001b[0m  ────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[13;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mconcept_id:\u001b[0m \u001b[0;1m44502762\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[14;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mName:\u001b[0m Large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma of ascending colon\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[15;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mVocab / code:\u001b[0m ICD-O-3 8013/3-C18.2\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[16;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mWhy it was missed:\u001b[0m It is a child of 761001, so it is missing for the same reason\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[17;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[18;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mHow I checked:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[19;1H\u001b[0m  1. \u001b[0;1mFull sweep of the anatomy hierarchy:\u001b[0m I took all 420 standard descendants of \u001b[0;1mNeoplasm of ascending colon (4130997)\u001b[0m,\u001