s why step 1 was the main check.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[36;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[37;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mWider impact:\u001b[0m 760999 sits at large-intestine level, so the same gap almost certainly affects the other segments, for\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[38;1H\u001b[0m  example primary malignant neuroendocrine neoplasm of the cecum, transverse colon and rectum. Re-rooting the build at\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[39;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mNeoplasm of large intestine (4130514)\u001b[0m and keeping only malignant concepts would fix every group at once. The filter\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[0m  would use ICD-O-3 behaviour /3 and SNOMED malignant ancestry or names, and I'd re-run this audit per region. Do you\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[41;1H\u001b[0m  want me to do that?\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[42;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[43;1H\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[0m \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mChurned \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[46;1H\u001b[0m❯ \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[48;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;38;2;255;193;7m⏵⏵ auto mode on\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m (shift+tab to cycle)\u001b[0m\u001b[K"]
