[0.1022, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[1;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mconcept_id:\u001b[0m \u001b[0;1m44502762\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[2;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mName:\u001b[0m Large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma of ascending colon\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[3;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mVocab / code:\u001b[0m ICD-O-3 8013/3-C18.2\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[4;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mWhy it was missed:\u001b[0m It is a child of 761001, so it is missing for the same reason\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[5;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[6;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mHow I checked:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[7;1H\u001b[0m  1. \u001b[0;1mFull sweep of the anatomy hierarchy:\u001b[0m I took all 420 standard descendants of \u001b[0;1mNeoplasm of ascending colon (4130997)\u001b[0m,\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[8;1H\u001b[0m     which covers every behaviour (benign, in situ, uncertain, malignant), and diffed them against the set. 54 were not\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[9;1H\u001b[0m     in either the included or excluded file. 52 of those are correctly left out:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[10;1H\u001b[0m     - 24 benign: 22 ICD-O-3 /0 codes, plus Benign neoplasm (442111) and Adenoma (46273188)\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[11;1H\u001b[0m     - 19 in situ: 18 ICD-O-3 /2 codes, plus Carcinoma in situ (4243742)\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[12;1H\u001b[0m     - 5 uncertain behaviour: 4 ICD-O-3 /1 codes, plus 4313363\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[13;1H\u001b[0m     - 4 hepatic flexure concepts that are benign, in situ, uncertain or unspecified neoplasm (4129878, 4241044,\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[14;1H\u001b[0m       4243126, 4315411)\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[15;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[16;1H\u001b[0m     The other two are the gaps in the table.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[17;1H\u001b[0m  2. \u001b[0;1mThe other direction:\u001b[0m all 117 included ascending concepts sit under 4130997, so none is misassigned to this segment.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[18;1H\u001b[0m  3. \u001b[0;1mHistology coverage:\u001b[0m 41 ICD-O-3 histologies exist at other colorectal sites but not at C18.2. I looked each one up\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[19;1H\u001b[0m     by code:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[20;1H\u001b[0m     - \u001b[0;1m1 is a real gap\u001b[0m: 8013/3, already in the table above.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[21;1H\u001b[0m     - \u001b[0;1m4 are non-standard\u001b[0m: 8000/3, 8010/3, 8140/3 and 8241/3. Each maps to a standard concept already in the set\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[22;1H\u001b[0m       (4247719, 4207182, 36713361 and 760958). One of them, \u001b[0;1m8140/3 Adenocarcinoma NOS\u001b[0m, is the most common colorectal\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[23;1H\u001b[0m       histology, so its records land on 36713361 \"Primary adenocarcinoma of ascending colon\".\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[24;1H\u001b[0m     - \u001b[0;1m36 don't exist\u001b[0m at C18.2 in this vocabulary.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[25;1H\u001b[0m  4. \u001b[0;1mName search:\u001b[0m I searched SNOMED by name for ascending colon and right colon. It found no other malignant concepts.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[26;1H\u001b[0m     The ICD-O-3 full-text search stopped at about 50 results, which is why step 1 was the main check.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[28;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mWider impact:\u001b[0m 760999 sits at large-intestine level, so the same gap almost certainly affects the other segments, for\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[29;1H\u001b[0m  example primary malignant neuroendocrine neoplasm of the cecum, transverse colon and rectum. Re-rooting the build at\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mNeoplasm of large intestine (4130514)\u001b[0m and keeping only malignant concepts would fix every group at once. The filter\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[31;1H\u001b[0m  would use ICD-O-3 behaviour /3 and SNOMED malignant ancestry or names, and I'd re-run this audit per region. Do you\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[32;1H\u001b[0m  want me to do that?\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[33;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[34;1H\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[0m \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mChurned for 2m 5s · done 7:01 pm\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[35;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[36;1H\u001b[0;38;2;122;162;247;48;2;28;46;82m❯ \u001b[0;1;38;2;255;255;255;48;2;28;46;82mCould we use the snomed morphology property to map backwards to ICDO3 and provide additional confirmation that way as\u001b[0;48;2;28;46;82m \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[37;1H\u001b[0;48;2;28;46;82m  \u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255;48;2;28;46;82mwel\u001b[0;1;38;2;255;255;255;48;2;28;46;82ml\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255;48;2;28;46;82m?\u001b[0;48;2;28;46;82m                                                                                                                 \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[38;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[39;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m The idea works if OMOP links the vocabularies in both directions:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[41;1H\u001b[0m  - SNOMED disorders carry morphology and finding-site attributes.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[42;1H\u001b[0m  - ICD-O-\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[43;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K"]
