60958). One of them, \u001b[0;1m8140/3 Adenocarcinoma NOS\u001b[0m, is the most common colorectal\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[19;1H\u001b[0m       histology, so its records land on 36713361 \"Primary adenocarcinoma of ascending colon\".\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[20;1H\u001b[0m     - \u001b[0;1m36 don't exist\u001b[0m at C18.2 in this vocabulary.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[21;1H\u001b[0m  4. \u001b[0;1mName search:\u001b[0m I searched SNOMED by name for ascending colon and right colon. It found no other malignant concepts.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[22;1H\u001b[0m     The ICD-O-3 full-text search stopped at about 50 results, which is why step 1 was the main check.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[23;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[24;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mWider impact:\u001b[0m 760999 sits at large-intestine level, so the same gap almost certainly affects the other segments, for\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[25;1H\u001b[0m  example primary malignant neuroendocrine neoplasm of the cecum, transverse colon and rectum. Re-rooting the build at\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[26;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mNeoplasm of large intestine (4130514)\u001b[0m and keeping only malignant concepts would fix every group at once. The filter\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[0m  would use ICD-O-3 behaviour /3 and SNOMED malignant ancestry or names, and I'd re-run this audit per region. Do you\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[28;1H\u001b[0m  want me to do that?\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[29;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[0m \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mChurned for 2m 5s · done 7:01 pm\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[31;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[32;1H\u001b[0;38;2;122;162;247;48;2;28;46;82m❯ \u001b[0;1;38;2;255;255;255;48;2;28;46;82mCould we use the snomed morphology property to map backwards to ICDO3 and provide additional confirmation that way as\u001b[0;48;2;28;46;82m \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[33;1H\u001b[0;48;2;28;46;82m  \u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255;48;2;28;46;82mwell?\u001b[0;48;2;28;46;82m                                     