;1H\u001b[0m  - SNOMED disorders carry morphology and finding-site attributes.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[35;1H\u001b[0m  - ICD-O-3 condition concepts carry histology and topography links.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[36;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[37;1H\u001b[0m  Checking which relationships actually exist on one concept of each kind.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[38;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[39;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mCalled groundworkers \u001b[0;1;38;2;153;153;153m2\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m times \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[41;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m I've identified two direct enumeration paths independent of hierarchy—ICD-O-3 conditions linked to topography C18.2,\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[42;1H\u001b[0m  and concepts with finding site \"Ascending colon structure\"—plus a morphology cross-check comparing SNOMED morphology\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[43;1H\u001b[0m  against ICD-O-3 behaviour codes. Next I'll run these enumerations and validate the matches.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[44;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K"]
