[0.0477, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[1;1H\u001b[0m     - 4 hepatic flexure concepts that are benign, in situ, uncertain or unspecified neoplasm (4129878, 4241044,\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[2;1H\u001b[0m       4243126, 4315411)\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[3;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[4;1H\u001b[0m     The other two are the gaps in the table.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[5;1H\u001b[0m  2. \u001b[0;1mThe other direction:\u001b[0m all 117 included ascending concepts sit under 4130997, so none is misassigned to this segment.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[6;1H\u001b[0m  3. \u001b[0;1mHistology coverage:\u001b[0m 41 ICD-O-3 histologies exist at other colorectal sites but not at C18.2. I looked each one up\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[7;1H\u001b[0m     by code:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[8;1H\u001b[0m     - \u001b[0;1m1 is a real gap\u001b[0m: 8013/3, already in the table above.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[9;1H\u001b[0m     - \u001b[0;1m4 are non-standard\u001b[0m: 8000/3, 8010/3, 8140/3 and 8241/3. Each maps to a standard concept already in the set\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[10;1H\u001b[0m       (4247719, 4207182, 36713361 and 760958). One of them, \u001b[0;1m8140/3 Adenocarcinoma NOS\u001b[0m, is the most common colorectal\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[11;1H\u001b[0m       histology, so its records land on 36713361 \"Primary adenocarcinoma of ascending colon\".\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[12;1H\u001b[0m     - \u001b[0;1m36 don't exist\u001b[0m at C18.2 in this vocabulary.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[13;1H\u001b[0m  4. \u001b[0;1mName search:\u001b[0m I searched SNOMED by name for ascending colon and right colon. It found no other malignant concepts.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[14;1H\u001b[0m     The ICD-O-3 full-text search stopped at about 50 results, which is why step 1 was the main check.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[15;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[16;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mWider impact:\u001b[0m 760999 sits at large-intestine level, so the same gap almost certainly affects the other segments, for\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[17;1H\u001b[0m  example primary malignant neuroendocrine neoplasm of the cecum, transverse colon and rectum. Re-rooting the build at\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[18;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mNeoplasm of large intestine (4130514)\u001b[0m and keeping only malignant concepts would fix every group at once. The filter\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[19;1H\u001b[0m  would use ICD-O-3 behaviour /3 and SNOMED malignant ancestry or names, and I'd re-run this audit per region. Do you\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[20;1H\u001b[0m  want me to do that?\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[21;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[22;1H\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[0m \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mChurned for 2m 5s · done 7:01 pm\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[23;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[24;1H\u001b[0;38;2;122;162;247;48;2;28;46;82m❯ \u001b[0;1;38;2;255;255;255;48;2;28;46;82mCould we use the snomed morphology property to map backwards to ICDO3 and provide additional confirmation that way as\u001b[0;48;2;28;46;82m \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[25;1H\u001b[0;48;2;28;46;82m  \u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255;48;2;28;46;82mwell?\u001b[0;48;2;28;46;82m                                                                                                                 \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[26;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m The idea works if OMOP links the vocabularies in both directions:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[28;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[29;1H\u001b[0m  - SNOMED disorders carry morphology and finding-site attributes.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[0m  - ICD-O-3 condition concepts carry histology and topography links.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[31;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[32;1H\u001b[0m  Checking which relationships actually exist on one concept of each kind.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[33;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[34;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mCalled groundworkers \u001b[0;1;38;2;153;153;153m2\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m times \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[35;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[36;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m I've identified two direct enumeration paths independent of hierarchy—ICD-O-3 conditions linked to topography C18.2,\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[37;1H\u001b[0m  and concepts with finding site \"Ascending colon structure\"—plus a morphology cross-check comparing SNOMED morphology\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[38;1H\u001b[0m  against ICD-O-3 behaviour codes. Next I'll run these enumerations and validate the matches.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[39;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mCalled groundworkers \u001b[0;1;38;2;153;153;153m2\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m times \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[41;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[42;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[0;38;2;177;185;249mconcept_neighbors\u001b[0m only follows edges in one direction, so I'll pull the topography and anatomy concepts' full\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[43;1H\u001b[0m  relation\u001b[0m\u001b[K"]
