[0.0477, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[1;1H\u001b[0m     The other two are the gaps in the table.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[2;1H\u001b[0m  2. \u001b[0;1mThe other direction:\u001b[0m all 117 included ascending concepts sit under 4130997, so none is misassigned to this segment.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[3;1H\u001b[0m  3. \u001b[0;1mHistology coverage:\u001b[0m 41 ICD-O-3 histologies exist at other colorectal sites but not at C18.2. I looked each one up\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[4;1H\u001b[0m     by code:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[5;1H\u001b[0m     - \u001b[0;1m1 is a real gap\u001b[0m: 8013/3, already in the table above.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[6;1H\u001b[0m     - \u001b[0;1m4 are non-standard\u001b[0m: 8000/3, 8010/3, 8140/3 and 8241/3. Each maps to a standard concept already in the set\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[7;1H\u001b[0m       (4247719, 4207182, 36713361 and 760958). One of them, \u001b[0;1m8140/3 Adenocarcinoma NOS\u001b[0m, is the most common colorectal\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[8;1H\u001b[0m       histology, so its records land on 36713361 \"Primary adenocarcinoma of ascending colon\".\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[9;1H\u001b[0m     - \u001b[0;1m36 don't exist\u001b[0m at C18.2 in this vocabulary.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[10;1H\u001b[0m  4. \u001b[0;1mName search:\u001b[0m I searched SNOMED by name for ascending colon and right colon. It found no other malignant concepts.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[11;1H\u001b[0m     The ICD-O-3 full-text search stopped at about 50 results, which is why step 1 was the main check.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[12;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[13;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mWider impact:\u001b[0m 760999 sits at large-intestine level, so the same gap almost certainly affects the other segments, for\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[14;1H\u001b[0m  example primary malignant neuroendocrine neoplasm of the cecum, transverse colon and rectum. Re-rooting the build at\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[15;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mNeoplasm of large intestine (4130514)\u001b[0m and keeping only malignant concep