[0.0115, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[1;1H\u001b[0m     The ICD-O-3 full-text search stopped at about 50 results, which is why step 1 was the main check.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[2;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[3;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mWider impact:\u001b[0m 760999 sits at large-intestine level, so the same gap almost certainly affects the other segments, for\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[4;1H\u001b[0m  example primary malignant neuroendocrine neoplasm of the cecum, transverse colon and rectum. Re-rooting the build at\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[5;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mNeoplasm of large intestine (4130514)\u001b[0m and keeping only malignant concepts would fix every group at once. The filter\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[6;1H\u001b[0m  would use ICD-O-3 behaviour /3 and SNOMED malignant ancestry or names, and I'd re-run this audit per region. Do you\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[7;1H\u001b[0m  want me to do that?\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[8;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[9;1H\u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[0m \u001b[0;38;2;153;153;153mChurned for 2m 5s · done 7:01 pm\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[10;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[11;1H\u001b[0;38;2;122;162;247;48;2;28;46;82m❯ \u001b[0;1;38;2;255;255;255;48;2;28;46;82mCould we use the snomed morphology property to map backwards to ICDO3 and provide additional confirmation that way as\u001b[0;48;2;28;46;82m \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[12;1H\u001b[0;48;2;28;46;82m  \u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255;48;2;28;46;82mwell?\u001b[0;48;2;28;46;82m                                                                                                                 \u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[13;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[14;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m The idea works if OMOP links the vocabularies in both directions:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[15;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[16;1H\u001b[0m  - SNOMED disorders carry morphology and finding-site attributes.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[17;1H\u001b[0m  - ICD-O-3 condition concepts carry histology and topography links.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[18;1H\u001b[0m\u