[0.1984, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[2;1H\u001b[0;38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[0m Yes. The morphology route works and gives an independent confirmation, and it caught one problem the hierarchy checks\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[3;1H\u001b[0m  couldn't see: \u001b[0;1msource codes for benign carcinoid tumour flow into concepts that are in the set.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[4;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[5;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mHow the bridge works\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[6;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[7;1H\u001b[0m  ┌────────────────┬────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[8;1H\u001b[0m  │  Concept type  │              Link              │                          Points to                           │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[9;1H\u001b[0m  ├────────────────┼────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[10;1H\u001b[0m  │ SNOMED         │ Has asso morph                 │ SNOMED morphology, e.g. 4029971 Large cell neuroendocrine    │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[11;1H\u001b[0m  │ disorder       │                                │ carcinoma                                                    │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[12;1H\u001b[0m  ├────────────────┼────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[13;1H\u001b[0m  │ SNOMED         │ Mapped from                    │ ICD-O-3 histology, e.g. 44498657 = 8013/3 (the behaviour     │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[14;1H\u001b[0m  │ morphology     │                                │ code is in the histology)                                    │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[15;1H\u001b[0m  ├────────────────┼────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[16;1H\u001b[0m  │ ICD-O-3        │ Has Histology ICDO / Has       │ Histology concept / topography concept 44498122 \"Ascending   │\