oncepts with finding site Ascending colon structure (234)\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[35;1H\u001b[0m  - This finds \u001b[0;1m761001\u001b[0m and \u001b[0;1m44502762\u001b[0m again. These are the same two gaps, now confirmed by a third method.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[36;1H\u001b[0m  - Everything else not in the set is in situ, benign, metastatic-to-colon (37168957, 4312150) or inactive lymphoma.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[37;1H\u001b[0m  - The one included concept that has neither link is 36715911 \"Primary adenocarcinoma of ascending colon and right\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[38;1H\u001b[0m    flexure\". Its finding site is the hepatic flexure (right colic flexure, 4168005), so it is still correctly in the\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[39;1H\u001b[0m    right colon group.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[41;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1m3. Behaviour check on the morphologies of the included SNOMED concepts\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[42;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[43;1H\u001b[0m  | Disord\u001b[0m\u001b[K"]
