9;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1m2. Concepts with finding site Ascending colon structure (234)\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[20;1H\u001b[0m  - This finds \u001b[0;1m761001\u001b[0m and \u001b[0;1m44502762\u001b[0m again. These are the same two gaps, now confirmed by a third method.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[21;1H\u001b[0m  - Everything else not in the set is in situ, benign, metastatic-to-colon (37168957, 4312150) or inactive lymphoma.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[22;1H\u001b[0m  - The one included concept that has neither link is 36715911 \"Primary adenocarcinoma of ascending colon and right\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[23;1H\u001b[0m    flexure\". Its finding site is the hepatic flexure (right colic flexure, 4168005), so it is still correctly in the\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[24;1H\u001b[0m    right colon group.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[25;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[26;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1m3. Behaviour check on the morphologies of the included SNOMED concepts\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[28;1H\u001b[0m  ┌───────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────┬────────────┐\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[29;1H\u001b[0m  │   Disorder    │                       Morphology                       │ ICD-O-3 histologies that  │  Verdict   │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[0m  │               │                                                        │         map to it         │            │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[31;1H\u001b[0m  ├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┼────────────┤\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[32;1H\u001b[0m  │ 435754,       │ Malignant neoplasm (37153816 / 4282379), Neoplasm,     │ (none listed)             │ Malignant  │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[33;1H\u001b[0m  │ 4247719       │ malignant (primary) (4312326)                          │                           │ ✔          │\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[34;1H\u001b[0m  ├───────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────