[0.0932, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[1;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mVerdict:\u001b[0m Malignant ✔\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[2;1H\u001b[0m  ────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[3;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mDisorder:\u001b[0m 1244590\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[4;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mMorphology:\u001b[0m Malignant neuroendocrine neoplasm (1242315)\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[5;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mICD-O-3 histologies that map to it:\u001b[0m (none listed)\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[6;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mVerdict:\u001b[0m Malignant ✔\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[7;1H\u001b[0m  ────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[8;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mDisorder:\u001b[0m \u001b[0;1m1077457\u001b[0m Well-differentiated NET of ascending colon\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[9;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mMorphology:\u001b[0m 1242311 Well-differentiated neuroendocrine tumor\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[10;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mICD-O-3 histologies that map to it:\u001b[0m \u001b[0;1m8240/0 Carcinoid tumor, benign\u001b[0m (36402243, deprecated), plus benign-carcinoid and\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[11;1H\u001b[0m  uncertain-potential carcinoid morphologies\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[12;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mVerdict:\u001b[0m ⚠ Mixes behaviours\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[13;1H\u001b[0m  ────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[14;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mDisorder:\u001b[0m \u001b[0;1m760958\u001b[0m Malignant carcinoid of ascending colon\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[15;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mMorphology:\u001b[0m 4174980 Enterochromaffin cell NET\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[16;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mICD-O-3 histologies that map to it:\u001b[0m 8241/3, plus \u001b[0;1m8240/1 Carcinoid of uncertain malignant potential\u001b[0m (44498804,\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[17;1H\u001b[0m  deprecated)\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[18;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mVerdict:\u001b[0m ⚠ Mixes behaviours\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[19;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[20;1H\u001b[0m  None of the ICD-O-3 histologies that map to these morphologies is /2 or haematologic.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[21;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[22;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mThe problem behind the ⚠ rows:\u001b[0m 1077457 is the \"Maps to\" target of benign carcinoid source codes:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[23;1H\u001b[0m  - \u001b[0;1mICD-10-CM D3A.022\u001b[0m \"Benign carcinoid tumor of the ascending colon\" (45537907)\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[24;1H\u001b[0m  - ICD-9-CM 209.53 (44821767)\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[25;1H\u001b[0m  - The retired SNOMED concept 760937\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[26;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[0m  Separately, 1244590 replaces the retired \"Benign neuroendocrine neoplasm of ascending colon\" (1246937). This follows\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[28;1H\u001b[0m  the WHO 2019 reclassification, under which all NETs are treated as malignant. In practice, though, records a clinician\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[29;1H\u001b[0m  coded as benign carcinoid will land in this cohort. The D3A.0xx codes cover every colon segment and the rectum, so\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[0m  this almost certainly affects every group, not only the ascending colon.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[31;1H\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[32;1H\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;1mDecisions for you:\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[33;1H\u001b[0m  1. \u001b[0;1mAdd 761001 and 44502762.\u001b[0m Three methods now agree on these two.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[34;1H\u001b[0m  2. \u001b[0;1mBenign-coded NETs:\u001b[0m choose one.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[35;1H\u001b[0m     - (a) Accept the WHO 2019 view and leave it as is.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[36;1H\u001b[0m     - (b) Drop the well-differentiated NET concepts (1077457 and the equivalents at other sites).\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[37;1H\u001b[0m     - (c)\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[38;1H\u001b[0m  2. \u001b[0;1mBenign-coded NETs:\u001b[0m choose one.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[39;1H\u001b[0m     - (a) Accept the WHO 2019 view and leave it as is.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[0m     - (b) Drop the well-differentiated NET concepts (1077457 and the equivalents at other sites).\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[41;1H\u001b[0m     - (c) Keep them, but exclude records whose source code is D3A.0xx or 209.5x. This needs the source concept ID in\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[42;1H\u001b[0m       the cohort logic.\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[43;1H\u001b[0m  3. \u001b[0;1mTopography-only codes (42511421):\u001b[0m decide whether to add a sensitivity analysis that counts these, since they never\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[44;1H\u001b[0m     reach a malignant concept.\u001b[0m\u001b[K"]
